{"alignments": [{"id": "ZEC.13.5.a001", "note": "The waw is rendered by “but.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a004", "note": "As the predicate of a verbless clause, the noun carries the supplied copula.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a006", "note": "The generic noun “man” is suppressed in the ASV's recasting as “a tiller.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.006", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a007", "note": "The participle is the predicate and carries the supplied copula and indefinite article.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a008", "note": "As the construct complement, the noun receives “of”; its anarthrous English phrase also supplies “the.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a011", "note": "The ASV's passive recasting uses the source agent noun semantically as the resulting status “a bondman.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021", "t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a012", "note": "The causative perfect is passively recast as “have been made.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t019", "t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a013", "note": "The object suffix is promoted to the English passive subject.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.013"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.014"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.015"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.5.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.5.016"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.5.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "ZEC.13.5", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "ZEC.13.6.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.001"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a002", "note": "The lexical subject “one” has no source nominal and cannot join the finite verb under the subject-pronoun permission.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a006", "note": "The interrogative is the predicate of the verbless clause and carries its copula.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a007", "note": "The ASV uses the explicit demonstrative rather than rendering this article.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.006", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a009", "note": "The article on the demonstrative has no separate English rendering.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.008", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.009"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a012", "note": "The ASV renders Hebrew “hands” as “arms.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.011"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.012"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a014", "note": "The waw is rendered by “Then.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.013"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a015", "note": "The ASV renders “say” contextually as “answer.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.014"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a016", "note": "The relative supplies its English antecedent and relative pronoun; the instrumental “with” belongs to the passive verb's recasting.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.015"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a017", "note": "The passive verb supplies “I was wounded” and the instrumental “with.” Assigning “with” to the English constituent “with which” is a defensible competing reading, but the verb owns the instrumental relation.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.016"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019", "t021", "t022", "t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a018", "note": "The adverbial construction licenses “in,” and the anarthrous construct noun licenses “the.”", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.017"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024", "t025", "t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a019", "note": "As the nomen rectum, the participle receives “of”; the ASV chooses “friends,” with “lovers” noted as an alternative.", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.018"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027", "t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "ZEC.13.6.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.ZEC.13.6.019"], "source_head": "WLC.ZEC.13.6.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028"], "target_head": "t028"}], "ref": "ZEC.13.6", "review_notes": ["The source reads “hands,” while the ASV has “arms.”", "The briefing records “lovers” as an alternative rendering of “friends.”"], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
